# Domain-level redirect (brucesbreads.org -> bruces-breads.com) intentionally
# does NOT live in this file. This file is shared by both Netlify and
# Cloudflare Pages (same repo, same public/ directory), and Cloudflare Pages
# does not support host-scoped "from" matching the way Netlify does -- it
# silently strips the hostname and applies the rule as a bare path match
# on whatever domain it's serving, which turned bruces-breads.com into a
# self-redirect loop (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS) on Aug 15, 2026.
#
# The domain redirect now lives in netlify.toml at the repo root instead --
# Cloudflare Pages doesn't read that file at all, so it can't cross-contaminate
# the two deployments again. See netlify.toml for the actual rules.
